__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.env
state.db
traces/
*.ics
# The rest of a home's runtime artifacts, matched by FILENAME rather than by
# the home's name. The `.syrup*/` rules below only cover homes we can name;
# one restored from a backup or pointed somewhere unexpected by SYRUP_HOME
# matches none of them, and its SOUL.md is exactly what you least want
# pushed. Keying on the artifact makes the guard independent of what the
# directory happens to be called — including names that do not exist yet.
SOUL.md
usage.jsonl
outbox/
.DS_Store
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# syrup is an installable package with loose, deliberate dependency bounds
# (anthropic>=0.40, ...) and 14 optional extras. A lockfile would pin the whole
# resolved universe — including the arena extra's mem0ai/langgraph/zep — and
# need re-locking on every dependency touch, for a package whose install path
# is `uv pip install -e .` rather than `uv sync`. uv regenerates it locally
# whenever it wants one; it does not belong in the repo.
uv.lock
.syrup/
.syrup.bak-*/
# Any ALTERNATE agent home, not just the default one. DISCORD_HOME gives the
# bot its own memory (see syrup/gateway/discord.py); SYRUP_HOME can point anywhere.
# Without this glob only `.syrup/` was covered, so a second home's SOUL.md,
# usage.jsonl and outbox/ were tracked — the exact files you least want pushed.
.syrup-*/

# Delegated coding deliverables (dated run folders + auto-run logs)
syrup_workspace/

# Scratch git worktrees the coding harness creates when it runs an agent in
# isolation — a full checkout plus its own .venv, so ~150M each. They recur
# every time an isolated agent runs and are disposable by construction: the
# work lands on a branch, not in the tree. Scoped to this one subdirectory,
# NOT all of .claude/ — launch.json and skills/ are tracked on purpose.
.claude/worktrees/

# Google OAuth: the client file you download from Cloud Console, and any token
# it produces. Nothing here should ever be committed — belt and braces, because
# the docs used to tell people to drop credentials.json in the repo root.
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
*token*.json
.gcp/
